<DemoExample Title="Basic" RazorCode="@example1RazorCode" CsharpCode="@example1CsharpCode" Id="example1">
    <div>
        Any class can feed the breadcrumb: NameSelectors maps its properties to what the component needs,
        either by a lambda selector or by a property name. An item with a mapped Href becomes a link, the
        item whose IsSelected mapping is true becomes the current page of the trail, and the IsEnabled
        mapping keeps an item in the trail without making it actionable (aria-disabled). A Target mapping
        opens the link in another browsing context, in which case the link is rendered with a rel of
        "noopener noreferrer".
    </div>
    <br /><br />
    <div class="example-box">
        <div>
            <div>Basic</div>
            <BitBreadcrumb Items="CustomBreadcrumbItems"
                           NameSelectors="nameSelectors" />
        </div>
        <div>
            <div>Disabled</div>
            <BitBreadcrumb Items="CustomBreadcrumbItems"
                           NameSelectors="nameSelectors"
                           IsEnabled="false" />
        </div>
        <div>
            <div>Item Disabled</div>
            <BitBreadcrumb Items="CustomBreadcrumbItemsDisabled"
                           NameSelectors="nameSelectors" />
        </div>
        <div>
            <div>Item Target (opens in a new tab)</div>
            <BitBreadcrumb Items="CustomBreadcrumbItemsWithTarget"
                           NameSelectors="nameSelectors" />
        </div>
    </div>
</DemoExample>

<DemoExample Title="MaxDisplayedItems & OverflowIndex" RazorCode="@example2RazorCode" CsharpCode="@example2CsharpCode" Id="example2">
    <div>
        MaxDisplayedItems caps how many items stay in the trail, the rest are collapsed behind an overflow
        button that opens them in a menu. OverflowIndex chooses where that button sits among the displayed
        items, so the first and the last steps of the hierarchy can be kept visible while the middle collapses.
        The collapsed steps open in a menu the keyboard drives: Enter, Space or the arrow keys open it, the
        arrow keys and Home/End move inside it, typing a character jumps to the item that starts with it,
        and Escape or Tab closes it back onto the button.
    </div>
    <br /><br />
    <div class="example-box">
        <div>
            <div>Max displayed items (1)</div>
            <BitBreadcrumb Items="CustomBreadcrumbItems"
                           NameSelectors="nameSelectors"
                           MaxDisplayedItems="1" />
        </div>
        <div>
            <div>Max displayed items (2)</div>
            <BitBreadcrumb Items="CustomBreadcrumbItems"
                           NameSelectors="nameSelectors"
                           MaxDisplayedItems="2" />
        </div>
        <div>
            <div>Max displayed items (3)</div>
            <BitBreadcrumb Items="CustomBreadcrumbItems"
                           NameSelectors="nameSelectors"
                           MaxDisplayedItems="3" />
        </div>
        <div>
            <div>Max displayed items (3), Overflow index (0)</div>
            <BitBreadcrumb Items="CustomBreadcrumbItems"
                           NameSelectors="nameSelectors"
                           MaxDisplayedItems="3"
                           OverflowIndex="0" />
        </div>
        <div>
            <div>Max displayed items (3), Overflow index (1)</div>
            <BitBreadcrumb Items="CustomBreadcrumbItems"
                           NameSelectors="nameSelectors"
                           MaxDisplayedItems="3"
                           OverflowIndex="1" />
        </div>
        <div>
            <div>Max displayed items (3), Overflow index (2)</div>
            <BitBreadcrumb Items="CustomBreadcrumbItems"
                           NameSelectors="nameSelectors"
                           MaxDisplayedItems="3"
                           OverflowIndex="2" />
        </div>
    </div>
</DemoExample>

<DemoExample Title="Icons" RazorCode="@example3RazorCode" CsharpCode="@example3CsharpCode" Id="example3">
    <div>
        Each item can carry an icon next to its text through the IconName mapping, and ReversedIcon swaps the
        icon and the text around (per item, or for the whole breadcrumb). The icon of the overflow button is
        configurable through OverflowIconName as well.
    </div>
    <br /><br />
    <div class="example-box">
        <div>
            <div>Item icons (OverflowIcon: ChevronDown - DividerIcon: CaretRightSolid8)</div>
            <BitBreadcrumb Items="CustomBreadcrumbItemsWithIcon"
                           NameSelectors="nameSelectors"
                           MaxDisplayedItems="3"
                           OverflowIndex="2"
                           DividerIconName="@BitIconName.CaretRightSolid8"
                           OverflowIconName="@BitIconName.ChevronDown" />
        </div>
        <br />
        <div>
            <div>Item icons (OverflowIcon: CollapseMenu) with active ReversedIcon</div>
            <BitBreadcrumb Items="CustomBreadcrumbItemsWithIcon"
                           NameSelectors="nameSelectors"
                           MaxDisplayedItems="3"
                           OverflowIndex="2"
                           OverflowIconName="@BitIconName.CollapseMenu"
                           ReversedIcon />
        </div>
    </div>
</DemoExample>

<DemoExample Title="Divider" RazorCode="@example4RazorCode" CsharpCode="@example4CsharpCode" Id="example4">
    <div>
        The chevron between the items can be replaced by any other icon with DividerIconName, or by a plain
        text separator with DividerText (the classic "/" of a file path, for example). Dividers are
        decorative, so they are always hidden from screen readers.
    </div>
    <br /><br />
    <div class="example-box">
        <div>
            <div>Default divider</div>
            <BitBreadcrumb Items="CustomBreadcrumbItems" NameSelectors="nameSelectors" />
        </div>
        <div>
            <div>DividerIconName</div>
            <BitBreadcrumb Items="CustomBreadcrumbItems" NameSelectors="nameSelectors"
                           DividerIconName="@BitIconName.CaretRightSolid8" />
        </div>
        <div>
            <div>DividerText (/)</div>
            <BitBreadcrumb Items="CustomBreadcrumbItems" NameSelectors="nameSelectors" DividerText="/" />
        </div>
        <div>
            <div>DividerText (›)</div>
            <BitBreadcrumb Items="CustomBreadcrumbItems" NameSelectors="nameSelectors" DividerText="›"
                           MaxDisplayedItems="3" OverflowIndex="2" />
        </div>
    </div>
</DemoExample>

<DemoExample Title="Templates" RazorCode="@example5RazorCode" CsharpCode="@example5CsharpCode" Id="example5">
    <div>
        Every part of the content is templatable: DividerIconTemplate for the separator, ItemTemplate and
        OverflowTemplate for all of the items at once, and a Template and OverflowTemplate mapped on a single
        item for a one-off. A template of an item wins over the template of the component.
    </div>
    <br /><br />
    <div class="example-box">
        <div>
            <div>DividerIconTemplate</div>
            <BitBreadcrumb Items="CustomBreadcrumbItems"
                           NameSelectors="nameSelectors">
                <DividerIconTemplate>
                    <BitIcon IconName="@BitIconName.CaretRightSolid8" Color="BitColor.Warning" />
                </DividerIconTemplate>
            </BitBreadcrumb>
        </div>
        <br />
        <div>
            <div>ItemTemplate & OverflowTemplate</div>
            <BitBreadcrumb Items="CustomBreadcrumbItems"
                           NameSelectors="nameSelectors"
                           MaxDisplayedItems="3"
                           OverflowIndex="2">
                <ItemTemplate Context="item">
                    <div style="font-weight: bold; color: #d13438; font-style:italic;">
                        @item.Name
                    </div>
                </ItemTemplate>
                <OverflowTemplate Context="item">
                    <div style="font-weight: bold; color: blueviolet; font-style:italic;">
                        @item.Name
                    </div>
                </OverflowTemplate>
            </BitBreadcrumb>
        </div>
        <br />
        <div>
            <div>Item's Template & Item's OverflowTemplate</div>
            <BitBreadcrumb Items="CustomBreadcrumbItemTemplateItems"
                           NameSelectors="nameSelectors"
                           MaxDisplayedItems="3"
                           OverflowIndex="2" />
        </div>
    </div>
</DemoExample>

<DemoExample Title="Events" RazorCode="@example6RazorCode" CsharpCode="@example6CsharpCode" Id="example6">
    <div>
        OnItemClick reports every activated item, no matter whether it is rendered as a link or as a button
        (a per-item handler can also be plugged in through the OnClick of the NameSelectors). Here the handler
        moves the selection, which the SelectedItem and OverflowSelectedItem styles pick up.
    </div>
    <br /><br />
    <div class="example-box">
        <BitBreadcrumb Items="CustomBreadcrumbItemsWithControlled"
                       NameSelectors="nameSelectors"
                       MaxDisplayedItems="3"
                       OverflowIndex="2"
                       OnItemClick="(PageInfo model) => HandleOnCustomClick(model)"
                       Styles="@(new() { SelectedItem = "color: dodgerblue;", OverflowSelectedItem = "color: red;" })" />
    </div>
</DemoExample>

<DemoExample Title="Customizations" RazorCode="@example7RazorCode" CsharpCode="@example7CsharpCode" Id="example7">
    <div>
        The breadcrumb keeps up with an Items collection that changes at runtime, and with the collapsing
        settings changing along with it. Add or remove items and move the two sliders to see how the trail
        and the overflow menu are recomputed.
    </div>
    <br />
    <div class="example-box">
        <div>
            <BitBreadcrumb Items="CustomBreadcrumbItemsWithCustomized"
                           NameSelectors="nameSelectors"
                           MaxDisplayedItems="@MaxDisplayedItems"
                           OverflowIndex="@OverflowIndex"
                           OnItemClick="(PageInfo model) => HandleOnCustomizedCustomClick(model)" />
        </div>
        <div class="operators">
            <div>
                <BitButton OnClick="AddCustomItem">Add Item</BitButton>
                <BitButton OnClick="RemoveCustomItem">Remove Item</BitButton>
            </div>
            <br />
            <div>
                <BitNumberField @bind-Value="MaxDisplayedItems" Label="Max displayed items" ShowButtons="true" />
                <BitNumberField @bind-Value="OverflowIndex" Label="Overflow index" ShowButtons="true" />
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</DemoExample>

<DemoExample Title="Truncation & Wrapping" RazorCode="@example8RazorCode" CsharpCode="@example8CsharpCode" Id="example8">
    <div>
        A trail of long titles is kept on a single line by default. MaxItemWidth truncates the text of each
        item with an ellipsis at the given CSS length, in which case the mapped Title of the item keeps the
        full text reachable as a tooltip, and Wrap lets the trail flow onto more than one line instead.
    </div>
    <br /><br />
    <div class="example-box">
        <div>
            <div>Default (single line)</div>
            <div class="narrow-box">
                <BitBreadcrumb Items="CustomBreadcrumbItemsWithLongText" NameSelectors="nameSelectors" />
            </div>
        </div>
        <div>
            <div>MaxItemWidth (with the Title of each item as its tooltip)</div>
            <div class="narrow-box">
                <BitBreadcrumb Items="CustomBreadcrumbItemsWithLongText" NameSelectors="nameSelectors" MaxItemWidth="6rem" />
            </div>
        </div>
        <div>
            <div>Wrap</div>
            <div class="narrow-box">
                <BitBreadcrumb Items="CustomBreadcrumbItemsWithLongText" NameSelectors="nameSelectors" Wrap />
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</DemoExample>

<DemoExample Title="Auto Collapse" RazorCode="@example9RazorCode" CsharpCode="@example9CsharpCode" Id="example9">
    <div>
        AutoCollapse measures the trail and moves the items that do not fit into the overflow menu, bringing
        them back as the room for them returns, so the breadcrumb always stays on a single line whatever the
        width of its container is. MaxDisplayedItems, when it is set, still caps how many items may stay in
        the trail and OverflowIndex still decides where the overflow button sits, so setting it to 1 keeps
        the root of the hierarchy visible and collapses the middle of the trail instead.
    </div>
    <br /><br />
    <div class="example-box">
        <div>
            <div>Drag the bottom-right corner of the box to resize it</div>
            <div class="resizable-box">
                <BitBreadcrumb Items="CustomBreadcrumbItemsWithLongText" NameSelectors="nameSelectors" AutoCollapse />
            </div>
        </div>
        <br />
        <div>
            <div>Overflow index (1): the first item stays, the middle collapses</div>
            <div class="resizable-box">
                <BitBreadcrumb Items="CustomBreadcrumbItemsWithLongText" NameSelectors="nameSelectors" AutoCollapse OverflowIndex="1" />
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</DemoExample>

<DemoExample Title="Structured Data" RazorCode="@example10RazorCode" CsharpCode="@example10CsharpCode" Id="example10">
    <div>
        StructuredData writes the trail next to the breadcrumb as a schema.org BreadcrumbList in a JSON-LD
        script, which is what search engines read to show the hierarchy of a page in their results. The whole
        hierarchy is written, the steps the overflow menu holds included, so what the crawlers are told does
        not depend on how much of the trail fits the screen, and the mapped Href of each item is resolved into
        an absolute address. Inspect the elements of the page to see the script the breadcrumb below renders.
    </div>
    <br /><br />
    <div class="example-box">
        <BitBreadcrumb Items="CustomBreadcrumbItems"
                       NameSelectors="nameSelectors"
                       StructuredData
                       MaxDisplayedItems="3"
                       OverflowIndex="2" />
    </div>
</DemoExample>

